    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize what I changed.\n\nThe acceptance test posts an owner with `title: \"DR\"` and `lastName: \"who\"`, then expects `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `salutation: \"DR who\"`. This is a Spring Boot / OpenAPI-generated-DTO PetClinic app, so I implemented the feature end-to-end:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema (documented as `MR/MRS/MS/DR`) and a read-only derived `salutation` field to the `Owner` response schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with the new accessors.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter so the title survives the create \u2192 read round-trip.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation(owner)` helper and wired it as a derived mapping: `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is absent/blank. (`title` itself maps automatically by name in `toOwner`.)\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `title` column to `hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, and `postgres` `schema.sql`. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema file is authoritative \u2014 that was the source of the initial 500 (`object not found: TITLE`).\n\nTest suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
